{
  "format": "marburgumii.street",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "status": "stage1_lent_street_people",
  "description": "Street people carried forward from the original Marburgum's ambient population: who walks Lent and its neighbours, where and when, how far off they appear and go, and what each personality does about a fight, a run-over, someone on the ground, being hit or being walked into, and which bus stops, cafés, shops and sights draw them in when. Mirrors MarburgumIIShared/Public/MarburgumStreetContract.h; `mb2 validate street` keeps them in step. Distances in metres, speeds in metres per second, times in seconds. Decision weights are relative, per column [stranger, player].",
  "provenance": {
    "source": "magna-raedarum-marburgum: UnrealMarburgum/Source/MarburgumServer/Private/MarburgumAmbientPopulation.cpp and MarburgumRunOver, docs/AMBIENT_STREETS.md, project/data/population_groups.json, project/data/npc_visual_profiles.json (population_groups.json `periods` and `zones` for the hours and districts, project/data/road_graph.json for every walk node's zone and activity and the attractors, population_groups.json `attractors` and the groups' `visits` for the places that draw people in; branches main, feat/ambient-react-to-bodies, feat/ambient-panic-spread)",
    "copied_unchanged": [
      "groups (archetypes, walk speeds, personality mixes)",
      "the night people group (archetypes, walk speed, personality mix) and its looks",
      "the workers and out-walking groups (archetypes, walk speeds, personality mixes) and their looks",
      "looks (profile colours and scale)",
      "periods, and every zone's street density and group mix by period, weekdays (the old town's day row with ADR-044's residents)",
      "decisions: body, attacked, bumped",
      "fight clearance, watch standoff, crowd spread, body notice and stand-by distances",
      "run-over strike speed, margin, damage per m/s and down time",
      "every walk node's zone and activity: the nearest node of the original's road graph (tools/build_road_graph.py classify)",
      "busy streets fill first: a newcomer is put on a street with a chance of its activity, at least 0.15 (TrySpawnPedestrian)",
      "each player's number from the zone of the walk node nearest them (Spawn, PedestrianDensityAt)",
      "the attractors: bus stops, cafés, restaurants, bars, fast food, shops and sights (road_graph.json, tools/build_road_graph.py load_attractors), each kind's action (wait, enter, look), dwell and how open it is per period, and each group's visit chance per kind (population_groups.json)",
      "visiting: one roll per node passed, at the place's node and the nodes joined to it within 40 m; three at most wait at a stop or look at a sight, 0.8 m apart along the kerb; a sight is looked at from 3 m; whoever goes in leaves the street; 0.3 of newcomers come out of an open door or are already waiting at an open stop (TryVisit, StepVisit, TrySpawnAtDoor)",
      "a venue's door is the point of its building's outline nearest the pavement (annotate_attractors), on Marburgum II's joined footprints"
    ],
    "marburgum_ii_own": [
      "decisions: fight (the original's row was San Andreas' shipped R_Norm/R_Tough/R_Weak values) and run_over (none in the original)",
      "people per player, spawn and cull distances (the original's were San Andreas' view bands)",
      "graph walking: continuous heading with weighted branches (the original used GTA III's 45-degree headings)",
      "fight notice radius 30 m (the original's 40 m was San Andreas')",
      "flee, watch and dodge timings",
      "colour and size variation within a look",
      "the weekend: Friday and Saturday evenings and Saturday and Sunday mornings one hour later, after ADR-066; nobody commutes at the weekend, the shops are shut on a Sunday and there is no school at the weekend, so those shares walk as residents; workers keep their shifts",
      "rain: what falls thins the street by 0.75 x precipitation",
      "going home: one unseen person every 2 s, the furthest and never within 22 m of a player, while more are out than the hour wants",
      "the night people's display name",
      "a walk node with no original node within 100 m is rural, activity 0.05 (the original's answer for a street with nothing near it)",
      "the workers' and out-walking groups' display names",
      "each place pinned again to this walk graph: the nearest node within 40 m (not on the carriageway) with a clear way to it, never across the carriageway, through a building or the river; the spot clear of the carriageway, the river and 0.45 m of every building, within 1.5 m of a venue's door; in the game, a spot that fails the level's check is tried up to 1.5 m nearer its node",
      "people already waiting at a stop appear whenever it is open (the original spawned them only 09:00-19:59, as San Andreas did)",
      "shops keep the 1990s shop hours of the lit windows and Kiosk 67: 07:00-19:00 on weekdays, to 13:00 on Saturday, shut on Sunday",
      "nobody goes straight back to the place they have just left",
      "somebody who cannot reach their spot in 30 s, or finds the river or a fight in the way, gives up and walks on"
    ],
    "excluded": [
      "San Andreas decision weights",
      "San Andreas spawn/cull bands",
      "GTA III wander, signal clock and car following",
      "crime points, pursuit, officers",
      "ambient traffic and carjacking (Marburgum II has no traffic yet)",
      "placeholder San Andreas / GTA III bodies",
      "the original's weekend (Friday 20:00 to Sunday 20:00, with its own tables) and its rain rule, which came in from a reverse-engineering report of San Andreas' population cycle",
      "each zone's police share (ADR-006: the police stay out)",
      "San Andreas' deficit fill of the group furthest below its share (a newcomer's group is a weighted roll, as ADR-044's)",
      "the zones' car densities and car mixes (no traffic yet)",
      "the original's 09:00-19:59 window for people already waiting at a stop (San Andreas' spawn hours for attractor users)"
    ]
  },
